---
import ContextZenOverview from './ContextZenOverview.astro';
---

<section class="zen-reading-overview not-prose" aria-labelledby="context-zen-reading-overview-title">
  <h2 id="context-zen-reading-overview-title">What should the next conversation inherit?</h2>
  <p class="overview-lead">
    A conversation may still fit inside a large context window while carrying abandoned directions, replaced decisions, and instructions that no longer agree. That does not make long context inherently bad. It makes room for a different question: would the next step be clearer from a faithful account of what is true now than from the entire chronology?
  </p>

  <ContextZenOverview />

  <section class="overview-section" aria-labelledby="context-zen-overview-state">
    <h3 id="context-zen-overview-state">Keep the state, not every turn</h3>
    <p>
      Context Zen proposes an opt-in, turn-time judgment followed, when useful, by distillation: reconstruct the current objective, decisions still in force, constraints, rejected paths likely to recur, active artifacts, unresolved questions, and immediate next step. The handoff carries that state into a fresh receiving context. It does not assume it can navigate to a new chat, and clipboard copying depends on the host. The complete operating loop and payload are in Full Research.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="overview-section overview-open" aria-labelledby="context-zen-overview-proof">
    <h3 id="context-zen-overview-proof">The continuation question is still open</h3>
    <p>
      The handoff specification is public and implemented; the Healthy / Watch / Handoff judgment is provisional. Length alone cannot trigger it, and no improvement has been established. To find out whether reconstructing state helps beyond simply shortening a conversation, the proposal needs a comparison against both the full transcript <em>and</em> a conventional summary. Different work may need different amounts of history.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="overview-continue">
    <p>Continue for the six figures, continuation markers, target-specific handoffs, and proposed experiment.</p>
    <button type="button" data-reading-depth-open="full">
      Full Research · ~5 min <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    </button>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .zen-reading-overview {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .zen-reading-overview :global(h2),
  .zen-reading-overview :global(h3),
  .zen-reading-overview :global(p) {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .zen-reading-overview > h2 {
    max-width: 42rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }

  .overview-lead {
    max-width: 46rem;
    margin-top: 1.1rem !important;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 1rem !important;
    line-height: 1.8 !important;
  }

  .overview-section {
    max-width: 46rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }

  .overview-section h3 {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }

  .overview-section p {
    margin-top: 0.8rem !important;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.95rem !important;
    line-height: 1.8 !important;
  }

  .overview-section em {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .overview-open {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    padding-top: 2rem;
  }

  .overview-continue {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem 2rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .overview-continue > p {
    max-width: 24rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.875rem !important;
    line-height: 1.65 !important;
  }

  .overview-continue button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    background: transparent;
    padding: 0.65rem 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.5;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .overview-continue button:hover {
    border-color: var(--border-strong);
  }

  .overview-continue button:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--accent);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .overview-continue button {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>